{"id": "g2_min_3v_minus4_remainder_two", "signature": "solve(codes)", "statement": "Given a list of integers `codes`, consider the entries whose remainder when divided by 5 is 2, using Python's % operator (so -3 has remainder 2 and qualifies). For each such entry compute 3 * entry - 4, and return the SMALLEST of these results. If no entry qualifies, including for an empty list, return None.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[0, 1, 3, 4]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[2, 7, -3]], "expected": -13}, {"args": [[0, 5, 10]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[12]], "expected": 32}, {"args": [[-3]], "expected": -13}, {"args": [[2, 2, 2]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[-8, -3, 22]], "expected": -28}, {"args": [[17, 27, 37]], "expected": 47}, {"args": [[1, 4, 6, 9]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[-1, -6, -11]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[7, -13, 2]], "expected": -43}, {"args": [[-2]], "expected": null}], "facts": [["arg", "codes", "int_list"], ["iterate", "codes"], ["remainder", "5", "2"], ["scale", "3"], ["add", "-4"], ["aggregate", "min"], ["if_empty", "none"], ["size", "codes", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["seq_fold"], "uses": [], "solution_sha256": "9af8ead50f449a78a745e79962bd9e1ec3ba7acd8373c05c70325c5b823d12d6", "reference_sha256": "fc8a4db2ab8070aa3a90adaffc34a7d822ff3596b47f82810bdd056f847e5ef3"}}